fter aside from expected chronyd/sshd PID churn from the reboot. Minor residue: /tmp/reboot.log (from the backgrounded reboot command) and the CA/leaf key material under /root/ca/oscomparison-root-ca remain on disk after the run, but both are low-risk, bounded artifacts directly supporting the task's created CA and its verification — not unrelated experimentation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ae691f52ad054540\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor created the 'OS Comparison Root CA' self-signed root CA on node1 and installed it into the system trust store via update-ca-trust, with direct evidence (trust list, ca-bundle.crt content, and a leaf-cert verification against system trust) confirming it functions as a trusted CA. The mandated node-restart evidence protocol was also fully and directly demonstrated: pre-restart healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, observed unreachability, a new boot_id post-restart, and confirmed persistence of both the CA trust anchor and functional verification after recovery.\",\"limitations\":[\"Executor evidence for the restart protocol is self-selected; independently, only boot-identity global observations (before_prepare and after_executor) are available as a cross-check, and they corroborate the boot_id change but do not independently re-verify CA trust survival — that rests on the executor's own post-restart command.\",\"No global observation set exists between before_prepare and after_prepare (alias/no-op since prepare was disabled), so preparer-vs-executor state separation relies entirely on the executor_comparison diff, which shows only expected reboot-related churn (boot id, temp files, socket PIDs).\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"ca-created","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority named 'OS Comparison Root CA' on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"op